course: dictionary
lesson: 4559
title: Hebrew: a language, a people, a describing word
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hebrew is a word with more than one job. It can name a language, the ancient language of the Jewish people. It can also name a people: in old Bible words, a Hebrew is an Israelite. The words around it tell you which job it does. «Workers in Egypt and Sinai spoke a language related to Hebrew» names a language.
explain: Hebrew can also describe something, which makes it an adjective. In «the Hebrew Bible», the word Hebrew tells you which Bible. A quick check: swap in another describing word, such as «the holy Bible». It still makes sense, so Hebrew is describing the Bible.
explain: Ask yourself: is the word naming something, or telling us about something? When you know the job, the meaning is easy. Hebrew is a noun for a language or a people, and an adjective for things that belong to that language or people.
fact: Hebrew is an ancient language of the Jewish people.
fact: Most of the Old Testament was written in Hebrew, so it is also called the Hebrew Bible.
fact: Hebrew is written from right to left, and its alphabet begins with aleph and bet.
fact: In Bible stories, «the Hebrews» means the Israelites.
fact: Modern Hebrew is the main language spoken in Israel today.
exercise: «Jewish children learn Hebrew to read the Torah.» What is Hebrew here? | A describing word for food | A place where people live | A kind of holy book | *A language
exercise: In Bible stories, «the Hebrews» means whom? | *The Israelites | The people who wrote picture-signs | The kings of the Nile | The Egyptian builders
exercise: Find and copy the word that Hebrew describes in «the Hebrew alphabet». | the | Hebrew | *alphabet
test: «The Torah is the first five books of the Hebrew Bible.» What is the Torah? | A Jewish school | *The first five books of the Hebrew Bible | A kind of Egyptian picture-sign | A river in Egypt
test: Which sentence uses Hebrew as an adjective? | *She studied the Hebrew alphabet at school | Hebrew is a very old language | A Hebrew is an Israelite | Hebrew is the language of Israel
exam: «Pharaoh ordered Hebrew baby boys to be killed.» Is Hebrew a noun or an adjective here? | Verb | Noun | *Adjective | Pronoun
